# ============================================================
# Markdown to PDF — frontend environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored) for local dev.
# In Vercel, set the same variables under
# Project Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# Architecture note: this project moved to a pure-frontend
# pipeline in 2026-05-13 (see docs/10-前端化架构补丁.md).
# Only the two Supabase variables below are actually required.
# ============================================================

# ---- REQUIRED ----------------------------------------------

# Supabase project URL.
# Where: Supabase Dashboard → Settings → API → Project URL
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Supabase anon (public) key. Safe to expose to the browser;
# Row Level Security on every public table is what keeps it safe.
# Where: Supabase Dashboard → Settings → API → Project API keys
#        → anon / public
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJI...your-anon-key...


# ---- OPTIONAL / LEGACY -------------------------------------
# Both variables below are read by frontend/lib/config.ts but
# are not used by any active code path in the current frontend-
# only pipeline. They are kept as placeholders for the case
# where the backend (Express + Puppeteer in backend/) is
# re-enabled. See docs/10-前端化架构补丁.md §5 for the
# re-activation trigger conditions.

# Backend API base URL (only meaningful if the Render/Fly
# backend is re-deployed).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:4000

# Public site URL (currently hard-coded in lib/seo/metadata.ts;
# uncomment + set if you fork to a different domain).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://markdown-to-pdf.app
